{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01781",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.86,
      "end_seconds": 4.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.57,
      "end_seconds": 13.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "You're alright, take a a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.31,
      "end_seconds": 23.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "Actually, mainly chest tightness when I walk uphill. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.48,
      "end_seconds": 27.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.22,
      "end_seconds": 30.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Ever since... since Friday, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.23,
      "end_seconds": 41.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.38,
      "end_seconds": 52.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.02,
      "text": "Yeah, it's worse with cold weather. It's all the time. I'd give it a four, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.52,
      "end_seconds": 56.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.96,
      "end_seconds": 78.15,
      "duration_seconds": 20.19,
      "text": "Breathlessness on exertion goes along with it, most of the time. The Breathlessness on exertion? That's been for five days. As for pain in my jaw, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.15,
      "end_seconds": 98.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.99,
      "end_seconds": 102.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "It's metoprolol, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.14,
      "end_seconds": 106.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.32,
      "end_seconds": 118.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "It's 50 milligrams. It's something called simv... simvastatin, 20 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.25,
      "end_seconds": 122.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.58,
      "end_seconds": 137.45,
      "duration_seconds": 13.87,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I'm on Seretide inhaler, twice a day. I'd been on losartan, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.95,
      "end_seconds": 153.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.22,
      "end_seconds": 160.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Ah, I have high blood pressure, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.51,
      "end_seconds": 162.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.07,
      "end_seconds": 181.27,
      "duration_seconds": 17.2,
      "text": "yes, high cholesterol my family kept telling me to get it checked i wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest i have asthma, for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.13,
      "end_seconds": 193.22,
      "duration_seconds": 10.09,
      "text": "Right, right. Alright, high cholesterol and asthma, that matches what I have here. A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.52,
      "end_seconds": 208.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.92,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.65,
      "end_seconds": 213.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "So, before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.2,
      "end_seconds": 217.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.44,
      "end_seconds": 221.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.6,
      "end_seconds": 225.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "my father has Parkinson's disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.81,
      "end_seconds": 243.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "and what about palpitations or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.37,
      "end_seconds": 249.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "I haven't had palpitations or leg swelling, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.64,
      "end_seconds": 255.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fainting or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.67,
      "end_seconds": 260.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I mean, no, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.37,
      "end_seconds": 265.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.86,
      "end_seconds": 269.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.87,
      "end_seconds": 275.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.07,
      "end_seconds": 278.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.37,
      "end_seconds": 283.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.45,
      "end_seconds": 294.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "bear with me while this finishes.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.19,
      "end_seconds": 318.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 119 over 68, temperature 36.7, saturation 99 percent. And heart rate 83."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.93,
      "end_seconds": 324.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.79,
      "end_seconds": 326.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.45,
      "end_seconds": 330.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.21,
      "end_seconds": 349.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Your heart sounds are normal and the the pulses are all present."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.24,
      "end_seconds": 366.74,
      "duration_seconds": 11.5,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Taking everything into account, I'd lean towards stable angina. It could also be gastro-oesophageal reflux, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.78,
      "end_seconds": 372.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.95,
      "end_seconds": 405.76,
      "duration_seconds": 31.81,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now stable angina is my leading thought, not anything worse. I want an exercise test done, that's for exertional chest tightness. I want an ECG done, that's for chest tightness. Let's use glyceryl trinitrate spray, 400 micrograms, when needed, long term. That should help with chest tightness. Stop and rest when the tightness starts, and use the spray if it does not ease in a few minutes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.72,
      "end_seconds": 423.37,
      "duration_seconds": 15.65,
      "text": "and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose the thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse if that happens, go to emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.2,
      "end_seconds": 427.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "That's fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.67,
      "end_seconds": 436.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "We'll catch up after the tests. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.05,
      "end_seconds": 439.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 440.78,
      "end_seconds": 442.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "take care now"
    }
  ]
}